Phase 2  —  Core Implementation  (May 22 – June 7)
Real work begins. Cross-dependencies appear. Pay attention to handoff dates.

Arjit  (May 22–31)  —  KV cache + state router
Implement S(cᵢ) = α·S_time + β·S_gps + γ·S_ble scoring function
TimeScorer: circular time distance + Gaussian decay
GPSScorer: Haversine distance + exponential decay
BLEScorer: RSSI sigmoid → R_ble reliability weight, M=0 → R_ble=0
KVCacheManager: serialize/deserialize KV states to flash (SQLite-backed), LRU eviction, top-3 RAM management
KV cache size cap: N=500 tokens max, INT4 quantized, ~2GB RAM budget enforced
Cold start recovery: BOOT_COMPLETED receiver + active sweep (GPS + clock + 3s BLE scan)
Two-tier fallback: Tier 1 SQLite generic response <50ms, Tier 2 async llama.cpp prefill

Medha  (May 22–31)  —  CNN-LSTM classifier
Train CNN-LSTM intent classifier on NinaPro DB5
Target: 5-class intent classification (confirm, reject, scroll, select, call-help)
Measure classifier inference latency on CPU (no GPU on Android device)
Produce labeled dataset: EMG windows + intent ground truth

Heer  (May 22–31)  —  Android app + fusion design
Wire context collection into ContextDaemon service
Implement GeofencingApi wakeup + BLE PendingIntent passive trigger
Implement AlarmManager for time-based wakeups
Design cross-attention fusion model architecture in PyTorch (waiting on Medha’s embedding spec from May 21)
